# Laguerre polynomial roots

The Laguerre polynomial of degree $n$ is

$$L_n(z) = \sum_{k=0}^{n} \frac{(-1)^k}{k!}\binom{n}{k} z^k$$

Its coefficients come from a loop, and `polyroots` finds every real root of the
polynomial in one call. The coefficients go in from the constant term up.

n: 5

>> #hide
>> a = vector(n + 1)
for k in 0..n:
    >> a.(k + 1) = (-1)^k*fact(n)/(fact(k)*fact(n - k))/fact(k)
>> #show

coefficients: a

## Roots

roots: polyroots(a)

>> #hide
>> p(x) = $Sum{a.(j + 1)*x^j @ j = 0 : n}
>> #show

Check that each root makes the polynomial vanish:

for i in 1..n:
    residual: p(roots.i)

## Shape

The curve crosses zero at each root.

plot p(x) for x in 0..14
